 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each part is one glass-passivated chip junction in a low-profile SOD-123FL case suited to pick-and-place assembly."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Polarity",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A band across the body sits at the cathode end."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Case and terminals",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The moulding compound is rated UL 94V-0 for flammability, and the case is RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. Terminals are solder plated and pass the solderability test of MIL-STD-750, Method 2026."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The full 2.0 A average current is allowed up to a lead temperature of 100 °C; above that it falls linearly, reaching zero near 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge over repeated cycles",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 50 A peak surge applies to one 8.3 ms half-sine cycle; the allowed peak falls as the number of cycles grows, to about 25 A at 10 cycles and about 11 A at 100."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Reverse leakage against voltage",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Typical reverse current rises slowly with applied voltage up to about 120 % of the rated peak reverse voltage and then climbs steeply. At 25 °C it runs from about 0.04 µA to 0.3 µA over that range; at 125 °C from about 4 µA to 20 µA."
  }
 ],
